{
  "comment": "Approved differences between the legacy transcripts and the settlement service. A scenario listed here is judged against its 'expected' block instead of the transcript and is reported as CHANGED (<change>) by make parity; anything else is still a FAIL. Each entry must name a docs/changes/CHG-nnn record (ADR-001, 'Behaviour freeze').",
  "transcript_rules_comment": "Which SPEC-SETTLE-001 rules each settlement transcript is evidence for, taken from the 'Observed:' lines of the spec. tools/traceability.py reads this to put transcripts and their parity verdicts next to each rule. An entry without a version (SETTLE-R05) applies to every version of that rule; a version-qualified entry (SETTLE-R06 (v2)) applies to that version only.",
  "transcript_rules": {
    "payment_issue": ["PAY-R02", "PAY-R14", "PAY-R15", "PAY-R16", "PAY-R17"],
    "payment_history": ["PAY-R18", "PAY-R19"],
    "settlement_bad_deductible": ["SETTLE-R06 (v1)", "SETTLE-R06 (v2)"],
    "settlement_blank_deductible": ["SETTLE-R05", "SETTLE-R10", "SETTLE-R24"],
    "settlement_calculate": ["SETTLE-R01", "SETTLE-R11", "SETTLE-R13", "SETTLE-R20", "SETTLE-R22", "SETTLE-R24"],
    "settlement_deductible_floor": ["SETTLE-R12", "SETTLE-R22"],
    "settlement_half_cent": ["SETTLE-R16", "SETTLE-R21"],
    "settlement_policy_cap": ["SETTLE-R13"],
    "settlement_save": ["SETTLE-R25", "SETTLE-R27", "SETTLE-R28", "SETTLE-R29"]
  },
  "payment_scenarios_comment": "Payment slice (ADR-002, SPEC-PAY-001): transcript_rules above also maps the two payment transcripts to their PAY rules, from the spec's transcript_rules block. The payment parity scenarios tools/parity/payment_parity.py replays against the payment service (ADR-002, 'How parity is judged'). Each scenario states its database precondition explicitly: the scripts under parity/preconditions/payment applied, in order, on top of the legacy seed by POST /parity/reset before the request, so scenarios do not depend on the order they run in. A scenario with a 'transcript' is judged against that transcripts/<name>.json. A scenario with its own 'request' and 'expected' has no transcript: both are copied verbatim from the legacy run recorded in docs/specs/SPEC-PAY-001-live.json ('observed' names the step), and 'expected.db_state' is read back through the service as for transcripts (payment.<id>.amount / payment.<id>.status via /payment/detail, payment.count.claim.<id> via /payment/remittance), plus payment.<id>.stored_amount / payment.<id>.settlement_id read raw from the parity profile's GET /parity/payment/<id> with the values of the live run's JDBC probe (12.345 unrounded, NaN, settlement 121). 'rules' are the SPEC-PAY-001 rules the scenario is evidence for, from the rule's Observed: line.",
